      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's understandable why you feel that way when you see patterns repeat, and it's true that cycles of pain can feel almost unbreakable. Instead of seeing yourself as a bridge, think of yourself as a point of intersection where the old story meets a new possibility. Even if the foundation has cracks, you can choose how you build the next layer, even if it's just a tiny, different one. Don't feel you have to fix everything; sometimes just surviving the current moment is a profound act of resistance against the pattern.",
      "source": "target",
